lator signals allow the elimination of the divide-by-four Johnson counter; described in Part 1, so that the DDS runs at the carrier frequency instead of its fourth harmonic. I have chosen to use the 200-MHz version of quency coverage requirements of dc60 MHz The DDS outputs are connected to seventh-order elliptical low-pass filters that also provide a dc reference for the high-speed comparators The AD9854 may be controlled either through a SPI port or a parallel interface. There are timing issues in SPI mode that require special care in programming. Analog Devices have developed a protocol that allows the mode to work around the serial Fig ~","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":341.0,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":385.6666666666667,"r":553.3333333333334,"t":583.2871511907043},"charspan":[0,761],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/3","text":"7 illustrates the Analog Devices AD9854 quadrature DDS circuitry for driving the QSDIQSE. Quadrature local-oscillator signals allow the elimination of the divide-by-four Johnson counter; described in Part 1, so that the DDS runs at the carrier frequency instead of its fourth harmonic. I have chosen to use the 200-MHz version of quency coverage requirements of dc60 MHz The DDS outputs are connected to seventh-order elliptical low-pass filters that also provide a dc reference for the high-speed comparators The AD9854 may be controlled either through a SPI port or a parallel interface. There are timing issues in SPI mode that require special care in programming. Analog Devices have developed a protocol that allows the mode to work around the serial Fig ~"},{"children":[],"content_layer":"body","label":"section_header","level":1,"orig":"About Intel Performance Primitives","parent":{"$ref":"#/body"},"prov":[{"bbox":{"b":277.3333333333333,"coord_origin":"BOTTOMLEFT","l":395.6666666666667,"r":544.0,"t":299.6666666666667},"charspan":[0,34],"page_no":1}],"self_ref":"#/texts/4","text":"About Intel Performance Primitives"},{"chil